// **the path an ordinary `echoc build` takes, which nothing used to be able to look at.**
//
// `-p` folds every unit into one module before printing, because that is the only thing an O3 pipeline or a
// single dump can see - so every IR golden in this corpus was asserting about the *whole-program* build, and
// the per-module one had no coverage at all. That is where Backend::optimize_unit runs, and before it existed
// the default build emitted completely unoptimized IR: every parameter spilled to a stack slot and reloaded
// per use, every accessor a real call - on the one path the object cache exists to serve.
//
// So this is the claim tests_eco/iteration/lowered_cost makes for `-O`, made here for `build` with no merge:
// the loop over an array is a load, an add and a branch, and the calls are gone.

function total(const array<int32>& $a) : int32
{
    int32 $sum = 0;
    usize $i = 0;

    while ($i < $a->count()) {
        $sum = $sum + $a[$i];
        $i = $i + 1;
    }

    return $sum;
}

array<int32> $xs = [1, 2, 3];

echo total($xs);
